      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A standard signalized intersection offers predictable, high-volume capacity when flow adheres strictly to timing plans, but its throughput suffers significantly from signal phases interruptions. Multi-lane roundabouts inherently manage traffic flow more organically, achieving higher capacity by continuously moving traffic, even if individual vehicle speeds are lower. During unexpected delays, roundabouts absorb 'friction' better because drivers constantly have some route options, whereas a stopped signal can cause cascading backups at traditional intersections.",
