      "content": "That makes sense. I'm particularly interested in those \"gradual breakdowns\" you mentioned. When you're looking at modeling these disruptions, how do you account for the non-linear nature of that friction? Like, what are the unpredictable or \"random\" variables that cause a flow to suddenly drop off even when the geometry is technically correct?",
